{"id": "EUVD-2026-71414", "enisaUuid": "473f096a-643a-3667-ba05-967f009abfd2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: nintendo: register input device after capabilities are set\n\ninput_register_device() exposes the device to userspace immediately.\nIn joycon_input_create() it was called before joycon_config_rumble()\nconfigures the FF_RUMBLE capability and the memless force-feedback\ndevice, so a concurrent EVIOCSFF could dereference a NULL dev->ff.\n\nRegistering early also means the initial udev event lacks button and\naxis information, which can make input managers ignore the device.\n\nMove input_register_device() to the end of joycon_input_create(), after\nall capabilities, the IMU input device and the force-feedback callbacks\nhave been configured.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:12:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:43:27", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3288bec1a21d582b504344380139cdc0e88ebe4d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/268679f501386ad46405d42c2bcf89384cb5e256", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9fc7547f911ada09da33c5e204e5acda38e765a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/27dc4b8eadac73b3c3cc526c8547d8b4ae8528be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d723bc1fe2e72b9252234e94c11af644ec477bf7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x6pf-56pg-q32p", "CVE-2026-80771"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20fe08ab-ae3e-3d7b-ac6d-a2791a20a8d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.1"}, {"id": "28826c3c-54f9-3bb7-8430-9dcdb67cf2b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.47"}, {"id": "37576e27-ddb1-3d8e-bd4b-00f8587e8d38", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "57a3cb87-fb4b-3835-9924-c95f709cefb3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2af16c1f846bd60240745bbd3afa13d5f040c61a <3288bec1a21d582b504344380139cdc0e88ebe4d"}, {"id": "5f8b9476-a7dc-36db-a637-11b5e68ce76e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2af16c1f846bd60240745bbd3afa13d5f040c61a <a9fc7547f911ada09da33c5e204e5acda38e765a"}, {"id": "60073ad5-a7a1-329d-b124-7276b010e8e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.11"}, {"id": "6b2f05ad-7d88-3867-8534-6947a1b70f3a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2af16c1f846bd60240745bbd3afa13d5f040c61a <27dc4b8eadac73b3c3cc526c8547d8b4ae8528be"}, {"id": "7b4ca776-5ff4-3a25-aae1-cf0403b27b60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "89a2c396-5a73-30d6-9566-83852e795019", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2af16c1f846bd60240745bbd3afa13d5f040c61a <d723bc1fe2e72b9252234e94c11af644ec477bf7"}, {"id": "c1fc082c-d1da-3b55-ac8c-95491ca42bcc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.16"}, {"id": "ca5c1ac7-10e7-31d0-82f3-73be512b798d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2af16c1f846bd60240745bbd3afa13d5f040c61a <268679f501386ad46405d42c2bcf89384cb5e256"}, {"id": "f4e50396-e66a-3d79-ac40-dbaba78b2648", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.106"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a76c41bd-2391-35f3-861a-03dddfea2a44", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}